         <sourceDesc>
            <source xml:id="src.ue1937" type="printed-edition">
               <bibl>
                  <title>Variationen</title>
                  <composer>
                     <persName auth="GND" auth.uri="https://d-nb.info/gnd/118629786" codedval="118629786">Anton Webern</persName>
                  </composer>
                  <edition>First edition (1937); the copy used was printed from the original plates in 1965 or later</edition>
                  <imprint>
                     <pubPlace>Wien</pubPlace>
                     <publisher>Universal Edition</publisher>
                     <date isodate="1937">1937</date>
                  </imprint>
                  <identifier type="plate">U.E. 10881</identifier>
                  <biblScope unit="page" from="6" to="6">p. 6</biblScope>
                  <ref type="digital-facsimile" target="https://imslp.org/wiki/Special:ImagefromIndex/28271">IMSLP file 28271</ref>
                  <annot type="copy">
                     <p>The copy used is the scan in IMSLP file 28271 (PDF of printed pages 3–11, SHA-256 d604c08ab797818f414a83fa4047eb2eb3c52ba6c74a47ce966e0a9c273ab330). Its first page carries the 1965 copyright renewal, so it was printed in 1965 or later; a first-issue copy of 1937 has not been compared.</p>
                  </annot>
                  <annot type="paratext">
                     <p>p. 6, head: page number "6"; movement numeral "II".</p>
                     <p>p. 6, foot: "U.E. 10881".</p>
                  </annot>
                  <availability>
                     <useRestrict>Scan uploaded to IMSLP by JacopoTore (2017); scanner unknown. IMSLP lists the file as “Public Domain - Non-PD US”. The page images are not redistributed with this edition; the facsimile links point to local renderings of the PDF.</useRestrict>
                  </availability>
               </bibl>
            </source>
            <source xml:id="src.kern.sapp" type="digital-encoding">
               <bibl>
                  <title>Op. 27, II</title>
                  <editor>Craig Stuart Sapp</editor>
                  <edition n="2020-11-23">Revised 2020-11-23; encoded 2008-12-17</edition>
                  <imprint>
                     <publisher>KernScores</publisher>
                     <date isodate="2020-11-23">2020-11-23</date>
                  </imprint>
                  <identifier type="file">webern-op27n2.krn</identifier>
                  <identifier type="SHA-256">79fb9a2c859e97eac5a959c28e21d177dc471d7d2c90312359a4201a644a5d1a</identifier>
                  <ref target="https://kern.humdrum.org/cgi-bin/ksdata?file=webern-op27n2.krn&amp;l=users/craig/classical/webern&amp;format=kern">KernScores</ref>
                  <annot>
                     <p>Base encoding for notes and rhythms, converted with Verovio; a starting point, not a witness. Its header notes: “encoding not finished”. Retrieved 2026-09-26 through kern.ccarh.org; not redistributed.</p>
                  </annot>
               </bibl>
            </source>
         </sourceDesc>
      </fileDesc>
      <encodingDesc>
         <appInfo>
            <application isodate="2026-09-27T13:26:44" version="6.3.0-425dd7b">
               <name>Verovio</name>
               <p>Converted the Kern encoding to MEI.</p>
            </application>
            <application isodate="2026-09-27">
               <name>Edirom Deep Optical Measure Detector</name>
               <p>Detected the bar regions on the page images (<ref target="https://measure-detector.edirom.de/">measure-detector.edirom.de</ref>); the facsimile zones come from its output.</p>
            </application>
            <application isodate="2026-10-11">
               <name>scripts/migrate_mei51.py</name>
               <p>Converted Verovio's MEI 6.0-dev output to MEI 5.1 by targeted text edits.</p>
            </application>
            <application startdate="2026-09-26" enddate="2026-10-11">
               <name>Claude Code</name>
               <p>Anthropic's AI coding assistant, used under the editor's direction for the facsimile linking, the MEI 5.1 migration, validation repairs and the draft of this header. Editorial decisions and responsibility rest with the editor.</p>
            </application>
         </appInfo>
         <editorialDecl>
            <p>This edition encodes the music as printed by Universal Edition, plate U.E. 10881 (src.ue1937), including stems, beams, clefs, the placement of marks, and page and system breaks. The Kern encoding (src.kern.sapp) supplied notes and rhythms as a starting point; it has no authority where it differs from the print.</p>
            <p>The print is not corrected. A suspected engraving error is kept and documented in an annot with type="editorial" and label "source-reading"; uncertain readings are labelled "unresolved-reading", and notes on the representation "encoding-note". Repairs that bring the encoding into agreement with the print are recorded in the repository's proofreading log.</p>
            <p>Every printed accidental is encoded as a written accidental (@accid); an alteration without a printed sign is encoded with @accid.ges. The values func="caution" and type="caution" left by the Kern conversion carry no editorial claim.</p>
            <p>Measure/@n is the printed bar number; the pickup of movement II is bar 0. Each measure points to its zone on the facsimile page; pb/@n is the printed page number. This movement still carries the page and system breaks of the Kern conversion. Page paratext is transcribed in sourceDesc; the pgHead repeats the printed head of the movement's first page for display only.</p>
            <p>The extent of proofreading is recorded in revisionDesc and in the repository's proofreading/progress.csv.</p>
         </editorialDecl>
         <projectDesc>
            <p>This edition was prepared by CAMAT Corpus Editions as part of a DFG-funded corpus for music-analysis technologies (grant PF 669/18-1).</p>
         </projectDesc>
      </encodingDesc>
